msgid "``em.graph`` — reading the graph"
msgstr ""

msgid "Generated for em API |api| from the docstrings of :mod:`s3dgraphy.em.graph`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Reading the graph — views, not nodes (SPEC-plugin §2.2)."
msgstr ""

msgid "``em.graph`` is the graph of the host (in an application: the one of the open document). What it returns are READ-ONLY VIEWS over s3Dgraphy's nodes: a script reads names, types, data, properties with their chain, relations, the chronology the core computes. ``node.raw`` gives the real node to whoever knows what they are doing — but changing it writes nothing (no step, no Log, no author), which its docstring says and a warning says the first time. Writing is :func:`em.write <s3dgraphy.em.write.write>`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bases: :py:class:`object`"
msgstr ""

msgid "The graph, read-only. Built over the live graph each time it is asked for (``em.graph``), so it always shows the host's current graph."
msgstr ""

msgid "``len(view)`` is the number of nodes (a new graph already holds its ``geo_position`` node); ``ref in view`` tells whether a node exists; iterating gives every node."
msgstr ""

msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

msgid "The graph's id, or None."
msgstr ""

msgid "The real :class:`~s3dgraphy.graph.Graph` (see :attr:`NodeView.raw`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "By id, else by name (the only one with that name); None if none."
msgstr ""

msgid "Return type"
msgstr ""

msgid "By id or by name. Two nodes with that name: :class:`AmbiguousNode` (use the id) — never the first one found."
msgstr ""

msgid "an id, a name, a :class:`NodeView` or an s3Dgraphy node."
msgstr ""

msgid "Returns"
msgstr ""

msgid "the node."
msgstr ""

msgid "Raises"
msgstr ""

msgid "no node has that id or name."
msgstr ""

msgid "several nodes have that name."
msgstr ""

msgid "Nodes of a ``type`` (``US``, ``property``, ``representation_model``… the node_type), with a ``name``, whose properties match ``where`` (``{quale: value}``; the value matches the property's value or its term's concept)."
msgstr ""

msgid "the node type (``US``, ``property``, ``representation_model``…)."
msgstr ""

msgid "the exact name."
msgstr ""

msgid "``{property name: wanted value}``; all must match."
msgstr ""

msgid "the matching nodes, in the graph's order."
msgstr ""

msgid "The relations of the graph, filtered."
msgstr ""

msgid "only relations from this node (id, name or view)."
msgstr ""

msgid "only relations to this node (id, name or view)."
msgstr ""

msgid "only relations of this edge type."
msgstr ""

msgid "the matching relations."
msgstr ""

msgid "``source`` or ``target`` names no node."
msgstr ""

msgid "The core's computation (``Graph.chronology``), nothing written: the whole graph's ``{id: entry}``, or one node's entry."
msgstr ""

msgid "One node, read-only."
msgstr ""

msgid "The node's id (unique in the graph)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The node's name (``US12``), or None."
msgstr ""

msgid "The node type of the datamodel (``US``, ``property``, ``representation_model``…)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The node's description, or None."
msgstr ""

msgid "The node's data — a read-only mapping over a copy."
msgstr ""

msgid "no step, no undo, no Log, no author, and in EMStudio the bridge throws the copy away. Use ``em.write``."
msgstr ""

msgid "type"
msgstr ""

msgid "The REAL s3Dgraphy node. Changing it writes nothing"
msgstr ""

msgid "All the properties of the node (``has_property``), as views."
msgstr ""

msgid "The value of the property ``name`` (a quale: ``material``, ``stat:fase_di_superficie``) — ``default`` when there is none."
msgstr ""

msgid "the property's name or property type."
msgstr ""

msgid "what to return when the node has no such property."
msgstr ""

msgid "The value (a copy, safe to keep)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The property ``name`` as a :class:`PropertyView` (value, term, unit, provenance), or None."
msgstr ""

msgid "The relations of the node."
msgstr ""

msgid "only relations of this edge type (``is_after``…)."
msgstr ""

msgid "``\"out\"`` (the node is the source, the default), ``\"in\"`` (the node is the target) or ``\"both\"``."
msgstr ""

msgid "the relations."
msgstr ""

msgid "The nodes at the other end of the node's relations."
msgstr ""

msgid "only through relations of this edge type."
msgstr ""

msgid "``\"out\"``, ``\"in\"`` or ``\"both\"``, as in :meth:`edges`."
msgstr ""

msgid "one entry per relation."
msgstr ""

msgid "One relation, read-only: its type and the two nodes it joins."
msgstr ""

msgid "The relation's id."
msgstr ""

msgid "The edge type (``is_after``, ``has_property``…)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The node the relation starts from."
msgstr ""

msgid "The node the relation points to."
msgstr ""

msgid "A property of a unit: its value, its term (when controlled), and the chain it comes from (combiner / extractors / document), as ids."
msgstr ""

msgid "The id of the property node."
msgstr ""

msgid "The property's name — its quale (``material``, ``stat:fase_di_superficie``)."
msgstr ""

msgid "the node's ``value``, else its description."
msgstr ""

msgid "The value (a copy)"
msgstr ""

msgid "The controlled term of the value (``{\"concept\": uri, \"label\": …}``), or None for free text."
msgstr ""

msgid "The unit of measure (``data.unit``), or None."
msgstr ""

msgid "The ids the value comes from (``has_data_provenance``), then what those combine or extract from — the chain, one level at a time."
msgstr ""

msgid "The property itself as a :class:`NodeView` (its relations, data, raw node)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bases: :py:class:`~s3dgraphy.em.errors.EmError`, :py:class:`KeyError`"
msgstr ""

msgid "No node has that id or name. A ``KeyError`` too."
msgstr ""

msgid "Bases: :py:class:`~s3dgraphy.em.errors.EmError`, :py:class:`LookupError`"
msgstr ""

msgid "A name given for a node is shared by several nodes: use the id."
msgstr ""

msgid "``.data[\"ids\"]`` lists the candidates. A ``LookupError`` too."
msgstr ""

msgid "The id a reference stands for: a :class:`NodeView`'s id, a node's ``node_id``, else the reference itself as a string (an id or a name)."
msgstr ""
